(window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS=window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS||{})["getting-started"]="<header class=\"mc-head\"><p class=\"mc-eyebrow\">Start here<\/p><h2 class=\"mc-title\" tabindex=\"-1\">Getting started<\/h2><p class=\"mc-lede\">What XZ Mods changes on the XDJ-XZ, what you need, and your first start from a prepared USB.<\/p><p class=\"applies\" data-applies=\"both\">Applies to <b>MODERN and CLASSIC<\/b><\/p><\/header><p>XZ Mods is software for the XDJ-XZ that starts from a USB stick. It adds a MODS menu, stems you can mute live, custom beat jump, four decks over a loopback cable, DJ profiles, themes and games. It can also replace the whole play screen with its own MODERN interface.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-what-changes-and-what-stays-stock\" data-anchor=\"what-changes-and-what-stays-stock\">What changes and what stays stock<\/h3>\n<p>XZ Mods runs in the player's memory. It never writes to the player's firmware, so the XDJ-XZ itself stays stock.<\/p>\n<ul><li>The player picks up the XZ Mods loader (<code>autoexec.bin<\/code>) from the USB at start and runs XZ Mods from there.<\/li><li>Your music, the library your DJ software exported and your playlists stay as they are. XZ Mods adds its own folders beside them.<\/li><li>The player's own settings are still there. Hold <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span> to open UTILITY, exactly as on a stock XDJ-XZ.<\/li><li>Settings you change in MODS are saved on the USB, so they travel with it to another XZ running XZ Mods.<\/li><\/ul>\n<h4 id=\"m-go-back-to-stock\" data-anchor=\"go-back-to-stock\">Go back to stock<\/h4>\n<ol class=\"steps\"><li>Switch the player off.<\/li><li>Start it without the XZ Mods USB, or with a USB that has no <code>autoexec.bin<\/code> on it.<\/li><\/ol>\n<p>The player starts stock. Plug the XZ Mods USB back in and start again to load XZ Mods. If you play from a separate music stick, that stick works on the stock player as before.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-what-you-need\" data-anchor=\"what-you-need\">What you need<\/h3>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Item<\/th><th>What you need<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Player<\/td><td>XDJ-XZ on firmware 1.26. No other firmware version is supported<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Computer<\/td><td>64-bit Windows with WebView2, or a Mac with macOS 14 or later, to prepare the USB<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Stems<\/td><td>Made on a Windows computer or an Apple silicon Mac. An Intel Mac can import stems made elsewhere<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>USB<\/td><td>A USB stick for the loader. It can be your music USB, or a separate loader stick<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Four decks<\/td><td>A USB-B to USB-A cable. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\" data-anchor=\"what-you-need\">Four decks<\/a> <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>The app downloads the official firmware it needs from the manufacturer and checks it. No firmware or boot files come with the XZ Mods download.<\/p>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--caution\"><b>Caution<\/b><p>XZ Mods is a preview. Test every new USB at home before you use it in a set.<\/p><\/aside>\n<h3 id=\"m-prepare-a-usb\" data-anchor=\"prepare-a-usb\">Prepare a USB<\/h3>\n<p>You prepare the USB in the XZ Mods app on your computer. It does not format the drive or touch your music.<\/p>\n<ol class=\"steps\"><li>Install the XZ Mods app and open it.<\/li><li>Plug in your USB. The app finds it and opens it. With several USBs plugged in, choose yours from the list.<\/li><li>Choose <strong>Install XZ Mods<\/strong>.<\/li><li>Follow the short guide: your DJ profile, the screen the XZ starts with, then a checklist of what it will write. <strong>Back<\/strong> returns to the step before.<\/li><li>Choose <strong>Write to USB<\/strong>, then <strong>Eject USB<\/strong>.<\/li><\/ol>\n<figure class=\"mf mf--app\" id=\"f-getting-started-1\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">XZ Mods app · Install XZ Mods<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/8e159d28e2145d12.webp\" width=\"1100\" height=\"760\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The checklist before the write. Music, playlists and prepared stems are never touched.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"52.727\" data-y=\"29.868\" aria-label=\"1: Loader\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-1-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"64.182\" data-y=\"35.921\" aria-label=\"2: Games\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-1-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"49.091\" data-y=\"41.974\" aria-label=\"3: Interface\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-1-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"80.909\" data-y=\"95.789\" aria-label=\"4: Write to USB\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-1-4\">4<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>The checklist before the write. Music, playlists and prepared stems are never touched.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-getting-started-1-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Loader<\/b> <span>XZ Mods itself.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-getting-started-1-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Games<\/b> <span>Free games the app downloads and checks.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-getting-started-1-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Interface<\/b> <span>The screen the XZ starts with.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-getting-started-1-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>Write to USB<\/b> <span>Writes everything in the checklist.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>Every step of the app is in <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"desktop-app\" data-anchor=\"usb\">The XZ Mods app<\/a>. To add stems to your tracks, see <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"stems\">Stems<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-first-start\" data-anchor=\"first-start\">First start<\/h3>\n<ol class=\"steps\"><li>Plug the USB into <strong>USB 1<\/strong> or <strong>USB 2<\/strong> on the top of the XDJ-XZ.<\/li><li>Switch the player on.<\/li><li>Wait for XZ Mods to start. Load a track as usual and check it plays.<\/li><li>Press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span> on the play screen, or touch <strong>MODS<\/strong> at the top right, to open the MODS menu. HOME is the first page.<\/li><\/ol>\n<p>If you use a separate loader stick, keep it in until XZ Mods has started. Keep the USB with your music and stems in while you play.<\/p>\n<h4 id=\"m-modern-on-first-start\" data-anchor=\"modern-on-first-start\" data-iface=\"modern\">MODERN on first start <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h4>\n<p>MODERN draws the whole play screen. The player's controls work as before, and the top bar adds a few buttons.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-getting-started-2\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODERN · Play screen<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The MODERN play screen with a track on each deck.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"96.500\" data-y=\"6.667\" aria-label=\"1: MODS\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-2-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"88.500\" data-y=\"6.667\" aria-label=\"2: STEMS\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-2-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"70.625\" data-y=\"6.667\" aria-label=\"3: DECKS\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-2-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"7.750\" data-y=\"21.875\" aria-label=\"4: Deck lanes\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-2-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"25.000\" data-y=\"60.000\" aria-label=\"5: Deck panel\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-2-5\">5<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>The MODERN play screen with a track on each deck.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-getting-started-2-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>MODS<\/b> <span>Opens the MODS menu, like a short press of MENU.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-getting-started-2-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>STEMS<\/b> <span>Shows or hides the stem rows.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-getting-started-2-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>DECKS<\/b> <span>Chooses two or four decks.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-getting-started-2-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>Deck lanes<\/b> <span>One waveform lane per deck, with its source and key.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-getting-started-2-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>Deck panel<\/b> <span>The track, time, tempo and BPM of each deck.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>The rest of the play screen is in <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"play-screen\">The play screen<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h4 id=\"m-classic-on-first-start\" data-anchor=\"classic-on-first-start\" data-iface=\"classic\">CLASSIC on first start <span class=\"tag tag--classic\">classic<\/span><\/h4>\n<p>CLASSIC keeps the player's own play screen and adds MODS to it. Touch <strong>MODS<\/strong> at the top right, or press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span>, to open the menu. A classic theme can restyle the screen. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"screen-and-themes\">Screen, interfaces and themes<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-choose-modern-or-classic\" data-anchor=\"choose-modern-or-classic\">Choose MODERN or CLASSIC<\/h3>\n<p>The XZ starts in the interface saved on the USB. You choose it in the app before the first start, and you can change it on the player at any time. Nothing else changes when you switch. Your settings, stems and decks stay as they are.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Interface<\/th><th>What you see<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>MODERN<\/td><td>XZ Mods draws the whole screen: bigger waveforms, a browse sidebar and a stems row with mute buttons. Marked Beta in the app<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>CLASSIC<\/td><td>The player's own play screen, with MODS added. Classic themes can restyle it<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>A new USB starts in MODERN unless you choose the standard interface in the app.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf mf--app\" id=\"f-getting-started-3\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">XZ Mods app · Install XZ Mods<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/65d78d7f49182700.webp\" width=\"1100\" height=\"760\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Choose the screen the XZ shows. New interface is MODERN, Standard XDJ-XZ interface is CLASSIC.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"44.182\" data-y=\"59.474\" aria-label=\"1: New interface\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-3-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"92.000\" data-y=\"43.684\" aria-label=\"2: Standard XDJ-XZ interface\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-3-2\">2<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>Choose the screen the XZ shows. New interface is MODERN, Standard XDJ-XZ interface is CLASSIC.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-getting-started-3-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>New interface<\/b> <span>MODERN.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-getting-started-3-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Standard XDJ-XZ interface<\/b> <span>CLASSIC.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<h4 id=\"m-switch-on-the-player\" data-anchor=\"switch-on-the-player\">Switch on the player<\/h4>\n<p>There are two ways to switch.<\/p>\n<ul><li>Press the button above <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.02\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LINK<\/span><\/span>. Out of the box it switches between MODERN and CLASSIC, and the screen says which one you are in. You can give it another job in <strong>PLAY<\/strong> › <strong>BUTTON ABOVE LINK<\/strong>.<\/li><li>Open MODS, go to <strong>SCREEN<\/strong> and choose <strong>CLASSIC<\/strong> or <strong>MODERN<\/strong> under <strong>INTERFACE<\/strong>.<\/li><\/ul>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-getting-started-4\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · SCREEN<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/cb5c523ef44bb366.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"INTERFACE is the first choice on the SCREEN page.\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/95a1b2af251c609a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"INTERFACE is the first choice on the SCREEN page.\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"25.000\" data-y=\"11.042\" aria-label=\"1: INTERFACE\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-4-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"24.875\" data-y=\"29.167\" aria-label=\"2: CLASSIC\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-4-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"41.125\" data-y=\"29.167\" aria-label=\"3: MODERN\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-4-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"45.000\" data-y=\"34.167\" aria-label=\"4: THEME\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-4-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"20.625\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"5: Explanation\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-4-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"89.375\" data-y=\"92.083\" aria-label=\"6: Save state\" aria-describedby=\"f-getting-started-4-6\">6<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>INTERFACE is the first choice on the SCREEN page.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-getting-started-4-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>INTERFACE<\/b> <span>The interface the XZ shows. The change saves to the USB.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-getting-started-4-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>CLASSIC<\/b> <span>The player's own screen with MODS.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-getting-started-4-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>MODERN<\/b> <span>The full-screen XZ Mods layout.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-getting-started-4-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>THEME<\/b> <span>The classic theme. See Screen, interfaces and themes.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-getting-started-4-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>Explanation<\/b> <span>What the highlighted choice does.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-getting-started-4-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Save state<\/b> <span>Confirms the change is saved to the USB.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--tip\"><b>Tip<\/b><p>You can always reach MODS with the hardware alone. In CLASSIC, the button above <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.02\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LINK<\/span><\/span> takes you to MODERN, where <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span> opens MODS, and the encoder and <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"back\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/back.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"76.49\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">BACK<\/span><\/span> drive it.<\/p><\/aside>\n<h3 id=\"m-updating\" data-anchor=\"updating\">Updating<\/h3>\n<p>There are two things to update, and they update separately.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>What<\/th><th>How<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>The app on your computer<\/td><td>On Windows the app checks at launch and offers the update. On a Mac, download the new version from the release page. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"desktop-app\" data-anchor=\"app-updates\">App updates<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>XZ Mods on your USB<\/td><td>Open the USB in the app. When it says <strong>Update available<\/strong>, choose <strong>Update USB<\/strong>. The app backs up the old loader first<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>XZ Mods over the network<\/td><td>Send the update from the app and download it on the player. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"connect\" data-anchor=\"updates-over-the-network\">Updates over the network<\/a> <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--caution\"><b>Caution<\/b><p>Updating the app does not change the USB. After an app update, open the USB page and choose <strong>Update USB<\/strong>.<\/p><\/aside>\n<p>Music, your exported library and your saved settings stay in place through an update. A USB built with <strong>Keep this version on the USB<\/strong> stays on its build and ignores network updates. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"desktop-app\" data-anchor=\"xz-mods-version\">XZ Mods version<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p>If something does not work after an update, see <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"troubleshooting\">Messages and troubleshooting<\/a>.<\/p>";
